smb: client: fix missed ses refcounting

jira KERNEL-814
cve CVE-2023-54076
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10
commit-author Paulo Alcantara <pc@manguebit.com>
commit bf99f6be2d20146942bce6f9e90a0ceef12cbc1e
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10/bf99f6be.failed

Use new cifs_smb_ses_inc_refcount() helper to get an active reference
of @ses and @ses->dfs_root_ses (if set).  This will prevent
@ses->dfs_root_ses of being put in the next call to cifs_put_smb_ses()
and thus potentially causing an use-after-free bug.

Fixes: 8e3554150d6c ("cifs: fix sharing of DFS connections")
	Signed-off-by: Paulo Alcantara (SUSE) <pc@manguebit.com>
	Signed-off-by: Steve French <stfrench@microsoft.com>
(cherry picked from commit bf99f6be2d20146942bce6f9e90a0ceef12cbc1e)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/smb/client/dfs.c
* Unmerged path fs/smb/client/dfs.c
diff --git a/fs/cifs/smb2transport.c b/fs/cifs/smb2transport.c
index ee4c7e55d361..8a6d1d4e7b4e 100644
--- a/fs/cifs/smb2transport.c
+++ b/fs/cifs/smb2transport.c
@@ -163,7 +163,7 @@ smb2_find_smb_ses_unlocked(struct TCP_Server_Info *server, __u64 ses_id)
 			spin_unlock(&ses->ses_lock);
 			continue;
 		}
-		++ses->ses_count;
+		cifs_smb_ses_inc_refcount(ses);
 		spin_unlock(&ses->ses_lock);
 		return ses;
 	}
* Unmerged path fs/smb/client/dfs.c
